# Dockerfile-specific ignore-file for viewer/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit prefers an ignore-file named "<Dockerfile>.dockerignore" living
# next to the Dockerfile over the context-root ".dockerignore" (the root one
# lives at /.dockerignore since the build context for this image is the repo
# root — see Dockerfile's COPY of both viewer/package.json and root
# package.json). This file REPLACES the root one for this build; it isn't
# merged with it.
#
# Two deliberate differences from the root .dockerignore:
#
# 1. It does NOT exclude `dist`. server/serve/html-inject.ts reads
#    ../../../dist/bridge-bundle.js at boot (an unguarded readFileSync — a
#    missing file crashes the process on startup), so that bundle must survive
#    into the build context. (Until 2026-08-08 the bundle lived under
#    `functions/serve/dist/` and the (now deleted) root .dockerignore's blanket `functions`
#    exclusion silently stripped it, producing an image that builds but exits
#    immediately on boot. Same hazard, new path.)
#
# 2. node_modules is `**/node_modules`, not `node_modules`. Docker matches
#    ignore patterns against the path relative to the context root using
#    Go filepath.Match semantics, so a bare `node_modules` excludes ONLY
#    /node_modules — `viewer/node_modules` and `editor-cli/node_modules`
#    would be copied by `COPY . .`, landing ON TOP of the deps installed a
#    few lines earlier and replacing them with whatever happened to be on
#    the build machine (including dangling symlinks, which is exactly what a
#    dev checkout using linked worktrees has). Same reasoning for .next.
#
# 3. EVERY pattern that must catch a nested path is written `**/`-prefixed,
#    for the reason spelled out in (2): Docker matches against the path
#    relative to the CONTEXT ROOT, and the context root here is the repo
#    root. A bare `.env*` excludes only `/.env*` — it does NOT exclude
#    `viewer/.env.local`, which is where an operator's GitHub App private
#    key, session secret, client secret, webhook secret and admin token
#    actually live. `COPY . .` below would then bake all five into the
#    image. (This was a real defect, found in the 2026-08-09 security
#    audit as B3; the `**/node_modules` note above had already worked out
#    the rule one line earlier without applying it here.) The build stage
#    now also ASSERTS no .env survived — see viewer/Dockerfile.
#
#    `.env.production` is deliberately NOT re-included: the image's start
#    command does not read a .env file of any kind (config comes from the
#    container environment), so an in-image .env is never anything but a
#    secret waiting to leak.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.git
.claude
*.md
**/.env*
# Runtime state directories — the viewer's default VIEWER_DATA_DIR holds the
# live SQLite database (sessions, machine-token hashes, comments) and the
# Editor's `.desde` holds chat transcripts and per-edit source backups.
# Neither belongs in a distributable image.
**/.desde-viewer
**/.desde
